# Netlify redirect rules — Garden Management
# Served from the publish directory root (this folder).

# ---------- Plant tag short links ----------
# A printed QR plant tag encodes  https://<site>/P/<tagCode>
#
# 200, not 301: this REWRITES to the app rather than redirecting, so the
# short form stays in the address bar and the path survives for js/main.js
# to read (absorbTagPath() turns it into the normal #plant-detail/<id>
# route). A tag is stamped into aluminium and buried in a border for years,
# so it gets a URL of its own with one line of indirection behind it — if
# the app's routing ever changes, these lines move and the tags still work.
#
# BOTH CASES ARE LISTED ON PURPOSE. The QR encodes the URL in upper case,
# because that lets the encoder use QR's alphanumeric mode instead of byte
# mode and drops the code from 33 modules to 29 — which is what makes it
# fit a label printer's tape at three printer dots per module. Scheme and
# host are case-insensitive per RFC 3986 and the browser normalises them,
# but the PATH is not, and Netlify matches paths case-sensitively. The
# lower-case rule stays for links typed or shared by hand.
# See docs/plant-tags.md.
#
# NOTE: index.html's own asset paths must stay root-absolute (/js/main.js,
# /styles.css, …) or they resolve against /p/ and 404 under this rewrite.
/p/*   /index.html   200
/P/*   /index.html   200
